  "scope": [
    "Add a deterministic, stale-safe publication command that previews and applies field-aware minimization of machine-local paths and private network identifiers in canonical Work Items, terminal runtime workers, completed tasks, and Evidence details without exposing matched values.",
    "Dogfood the command on Temple's current canonical state and record a value-redacted manifest that preserves lifecycle, Evidence identity, revision, artifact digest, and audit history.",
    "Keep retained artifact normalization, first-party and vendored fixture cleanup, historical Git rewriting, visibility, version, tag, Release, npm, and announcement outside this Work Item."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Preview is read-only, value-redacted, stable for unchanged inputs, and bound to a plan digest; apply requires the exact current plan and explicit confirmation.",
    "Only released Work Item claims, terminal runtime workers, terminal tasks, and allowlisted local-environment fields in Evidence details are minimized; active execution coordinates and evidence artifact paths are never changed.",
    "Apply is atomic, idempotent, schema-valid, audit-event bearing, and reduces the canonical-state publication findings from 245 occurrences to zero without changing Evidence IDs or artifact digests.",
    "Full verification and Independent QA pass at an exact candidate; no publication or history rewrite occurs."
  ],
